  "body": "Elevated on a quiet Orakei ridge and held with care by the same owners for more than 12 years, this classic 1960s single-level weatherboard home brings together enduring character, effortless entertaining and genuine privacy in one of the Eastern Bays' most connected pockets.\r\n\r\nTucked back off the street behind lush manicured hedging, the home welcomes you through a slatted pergola entrance onto an expansive, sun-drenched front deck rebuilt in summer 2025. Framed by fragrant gardenia and jasmine, it is a space built for long evenings, pink-sky sunsets and easy hosting, with views reaching across the Orakei Basin to Mt Eden, Mt Hobson, Mt St John and the Sky Tower.\r\n\r\nInside, gleaming native timber floors run throughout a light-filled layout that works naturally for everyday life. French doors open directly from both the living room and the master bedroom onto the front deck, letting late-afternoon sun pour straight into the home. Flowing off the living space, the remodelled white kitchen pairs clean modern lines with a sunny eat-in dining area, stepping through to a separate laundry and a second, sheltered rear deck.\r\n\r\n* Three generous bedrooms, all with built-in wardrobes and native timber floors, including a sun-catching master opening straight to the front deck and a versatile third bedroom suited to a nursery, child's room or work-from-home office.\r\n\r\n* Remodelled modern eat-in kitchen featuring sleek cabinetry, matte black tapware, splashback, quality appliances and direct flow through the living area to outdoor dining.\r\n\r\n* Dual outdoor living zones: an expansive north-west facing front entertaining deck for sunset BBQs and gatherings, plus a sheltered rear deck stepping down to a private, flat, fully fenced back lawn framed by established subtropical planting, a summer-flowering pink Crepe Myrtle and fruiting feijoa trees.\r\n\r\n* Year-round comfort sorted with generous wool ceiling insulation and four heat pumps positioned through the home.\r\n\r\n* Tidy tiled family bathroom with shower-over-bath, modern vanity and separate laundry room opening straight to the rear deck.\r\n\r\n* Single covered carport and tucked-away privacy on a quiet street where through-traffic stays on the edges.\r\n\r\nLife in this pocket of Orakei is remarkably easy. Grab your morning coffee at neighbourhood favourite Good Day cafe along Coates Avenue, pick up essentials at Eastridge Shopping Centre just down Kepa Road, or head down to Orakei Bay Village and the Orakei Train Station, where the City Rail Link puts the CBD, uptown and Eden Park within effortless direct reach. Weekends write themselves with the 2.9km Orakei Basin walkway, Hobson Bay Walkway, Kupe Reserve, Kepa Bush Reserve, Orakei Tennis Club, Orakei Domain and Okahu Bay all close by, plus Mission Bay, Kohimarama and St Heliers beaches just minutes down the road.\r\n\r\nFor more than a decade, our owners have loved raising their young family here, from quiet afternoon coffees on the deck to hosting their annual street-side Christmas BBQ for 30+ friends. Having already purchased and upsized for their growing family, their instructions are clear - creating a rare opportunity to secure a classic 1960s bit of Kiwiana charm in a tightly held Eastern Bays address.\r\n\r\nYour earliest inspection is recommended. Call Team Frazer MJ today.",
